message: "If you use engrheo in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "engrheo: rheology for engineers in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Yanwei
    email: wangyanwei@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8488-9833"
    website: "https://github.com/ktwyw"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ktwyw/engrheo"
keywords:
  - rheology
  - non-Newtonian fluids
  - viscoelasticity
  - rheometry
  - engineering education
abstract: >-
  Readable, validated Python for engineering rheology - flow-curve models and fitting with uncertainties,
  rheometer corrections, time-temperature superposition, linear and nonlinear viscoelasticity (spectra,
  Giesekus and PTT models, LAOS), thixotropy, suspensions, extensional rheology, and pipe flow, mixing
  and extrusion of non-Newtonian fluids - checked against exact solutions, with an 18-notebook course and
  worked solutions for students and practising engineers.
